OVERVIEW
--------
PARSIFAL is a C++/ROOT parameterized Monte Carlo simulator for Micro-Pattern
Gaseous Detectors (MPGDs), supporting:
  - Detectors : u-RWELL (Planar 1D, default), triple-GEM (Planar 2D), uRTube (R-Phi)
  - ASICs     : APV (0), TIGER (1), TORA (2)
  - Pipeline  : Primary/secondary ionization -> electron drift & diffusion ->
                detector gain -> fast/slow ion-tail induction -> resistive
                charge dispersion (T2K+Shepherd) -> white noise with pre-t0
                buffer -> optional FFT bandpass filter -> shaper convolution ->
                saturation & digitization -> hit/cluster CC & uTPC reconstruction
  - Parallelism: OpenMP multi-threading (compiled with -O2 -fopenmp)

BRANCHES
--------
  - triplegem   : Legacy triple-GEM simulation
  - main        : u-RWELL simulation with ion tail, T2K resistive model, white noise, OpenMP
  - Tora        : TORA ASIC integration, FFT filtering, independent rise/trail thresholds,
                  APV and TIGER experimental tuning
  - Parsifal-AI : Physics/OpenMP/ROOT bugfixes, Waveform & kernel optimizations,
                  runtime CLI flags, -MMD -MP build, info_sim_angle<deg>.txt
                  reports, parametric HVscan.C, deterministic regression tests

REQUIREMENTS
------------
  - ROOT 6 (https://root.cern.ch/) with C++17 support
  - g++ with OpenMP support (-fopenmp)

HOWTO (BUILD & RUN)
-------------------
  1) Load ROOT environment:
       source $ROOTSYS/bin/thisroot.sh
  2) Enter the PARSIFAL directory:
       cd /path/to/PARSIFAL
  3) Initialize local environment script (generates bash_PARSIFAL):
       source init_PARSIFAL.sh
  4) Load PARSIFAL environment variables and aliases:
       source bash_PARSIFAL
  5) Compile Simulate and Analysis (Makefile tracks .h dependencies via -MMD -MP):
       parsifal -m       (incremental build)
       parsifal -M       (full clean rebuild)
  6) Display available wrapper options:
       parsifal -h
  7) Run a simulation + analysis (example 1-event sanity runs at 0 deg):
       parsifal -S 2 0   (APV)
       parsifal -S 1 0   (TIGER)
       parsifal -S 0 0   (TORA)
  8) Run with runtime CLI overrides (no recompilation needed):
       ./bin/Simulate 36 0 --nevents 100 --seed 12345 --no-noise 0 --tora-shaper 1
  9) Run analysis only or open output ROOT file:
       parsifal -A <runID> [angle]
       parsifal -O <runID> <angle>
  10) Run deterministic 3-ASIC regression test suite (APV, TIGER, TORA):
       bash tests/regression_test.sh
  11) Produce HV scan comparison plots against experimental APV/TIGER data:
       root -l -b -q 'src/Plot/HVscan.C("APV","data","pdf")'
       root -l -b -q 'src/Plot/HVscan.C("TIGER","data","pdf")'

CONFIGURATION (run_list.txt)
----------------------------
Each numeric row in run_list.txt defines a run configuration with 24 columns:
  0  Run             Run ID
  1  nEvt            Number of simulated events
  2  GainFctr        Detector gain tuning factor
  3  SpaceDiffFctr   Spatial diffusion tuning factor
  4  TimeDiffFctr    Temporal diffusion tuning factor
  5  Res_RC          Resistive RC time constant [ns]
  6  Res_Sigma0      Resistive initial spread sigma0 [mm]
  7  DetGain         Mean detector gain
  8  Noise_fC        Input noise level [fC]
  9  Thr_fC          General charge threshold [fC]
  10 IT_Length       Ion tail duration [ns]
  11 IT_ratio        Slow (ion) fraction of total induced signal
  12 APV_ped         APV pedestal standard deviation
  13 APV_thr         APV threshold multiplier
  14 TIGER_E_fC_thr  TIGER energy-branch threshold [fC]
  15 TIGER_T_fC_thr  TIGER time-branch threshold [fC]
  16 TORA_thr_rise   TORA rising-edge threshold [fC]
  17 TORA_thr_trail  TORA trailing-edge threshold [fC]
  18 TORA_gain       TORA front-end gain [mV/fC]
  19 TORA_tau        TORA shaping/peaking time tau [ns]
  20 FFT_fmin        FFT high-pass cutoff [Hz] (0 = disabled)
  21 FFT_fmax        FFT low-pass cutoff [Hz]  (0 = disabled)
  22 Electronics     ASIC code (0 = APV, 1 = TIGER, 2 = TORA)
  23 Strip_Pitch     Readout strip pitch [mm]

RUNTIME CLI FLAGS & DEFAULT SWITCHES
------------------------------------
  - CLI overrides (./bin/Simulate <runID> <angle> [options]):
      --seed <U>          Deterministic RNG seed (0 = random)
      --nevents <N>       Override event count from run_list.txt
      --bfield <0|1>      Enable/disable magnetic field
      --no-noise <0|1>    Disable/enable noise
      --no-sat <0|1>      Disable/enable saturation
      --no-fft <0|1>      Disable/enable FFT filter
      --plot-hits <0|1>   Save PDF/PNG waveforms for hits above threshold
      --tora-shaper <1|3> Select TORA shaper order (1 or 3)
  - Default switches in src/Common/Common.h:
      NO_PrimaryIonization, NO_SecondaryIonization, NO_Gain, NO_Drift,
      NO_Resistive, NO_Readout, NO_Saturation, NO_Noise, NO_FFT,
      NO_Capacitive, NO_Hit, NO_Cluster, NO_uTPC_Correction, NO_Ion_Tail
      (set to false to enable the corresponding stage; true to bypass it),
      fast_simulation (true recommended), Bfield, SEED, TORA_shaper_order,
      Print_Plot_Above_Thr (false by default), n_ns, n_ns_buffer.

OUTPUT FILES (data/<runID>/)
----------------------------
  - run_angle<deg>.root       : ROOT TTree ("tree") with ionization, channel,
                                hit, and 1D cluster branches.
  - info_sim_angle<deg>.txt   : Human-readable report with timestamps, runtime,
                                decoded run_list.txt parameters, and flags.
  - summary.txt               : Reconstructed metrics (Angle, Qind MPV, Qread,
                                RatioQ, Size, CCres, TPCres, T0res, Eff).

KNOWN LIMITATIONS & FUTURE UPGRADES
-----------------------------------
  - Finalize TORA front-end charge/time extraction in Readout::Get_Charge_TORA.
  - Ionization tables currently cover muons in Ar:iC4H10 (90:10) and
    Ar:CO2:CF4 (45:15:40); extend to additional particles/gas mixtures.
  - Allow runtime selection of detector setup (triple-GEM / u-RWELL / uRTube)
    without recompiling.
  - See ChangeLog and README.md for the full chronological history.
